# Copy to ~/.config/job-tracker/backup.env (mode 600).
#
# Only the bucket name lives here. The B2 application key goes in
# ~/.config/job-tracker/rclone.conf and the encryption passphrase in
# ~/.config/job-tracker/backup.pass -- both also mode 600, both written with
# `read -s` so they never enter shell history.
#
# The passphrase must also exist somewhere off this machine (a password
# manager). A key stored only on the server it protects dies with it, and every
# off-site copy becomes unreadable at exactly the moment it is needed.
B2_BUCKET=job-tracker-backups-changeme
